   1758  fabb							; (PairGone RETIRED, plan 5.1b 2026-10-20: the cell punch guards a repeat
   1759  fabb							;  blast on the PF buffer itself — the punched cell pair is empty, so a
   1760  fabb							;  second blast in the same room cannot score again. No rect idx4, no mask.)
   1761  fabb
   1762  fabb							; ========================================================================
   1763  fabb							; BombMarkWalls (S5.2, moved from bank0) — pinned at $FB10.
   1764  fabb							;   On the bomb 1->2 edge: punch the THIN walls in the blast window and
   1765  fabb							;   report how many were newly broken (A, caller scores +75 each).
   1766  fabb							;   Bomb left-half col +-2, clamped 0..19. Score is NOT done here — pads
   1767  fabb							;   cannot nest (ReturnPad switches to bank0), so the bank0 caller adds
   1768  fabb							;   +75 per wall.
   1769  fabb							;   Plan 5.1b (2026-10-20): the punch is CELL-based — no rect cache. The
   1770  fabb							;   PF buffers ARE the map (export: convert_room.pf_values; holes included),
   1771  fabb							;   so a bombable wall is found the same way find_rectangles finds a w==2
   1772  fabb							;   rect: a thin wall is ONE D7 logical cell = 2 display cols = a solid
   1773  fabb							;   PF bit-PAIR whose left and right neighbouring cells are empty. The
   1774  fabb							;   emitted cells are pair-aligned (both bits of a cell are always written
   1775  fabb							;   together: pf_values, ClearPFColumn, PhMaskTab), so ONE solidity read
   1776  fabb							;   per cell covers both cols, and vertical extent needs no data: each row
   1777  fabb							;   is tested on its own (the old rect h is exactly the run of thin rows —
   1778  fabb							;   find_rectangles stops a w==1 rect at a row that joins a wider run, and
   1779  fabb							;   so does the neighbour test). Col 0 (screen border, and its mirror col
   1780  fabb							;   39) is never destroyable — the old `rect.x == 0` skip.
   1781  fabb							;   Double-score guard = the buffer: the punched pair is empty, so a second
   1782  fabb							;   blast in the same room finds no cell (the old WallMask bits and PairGone
   1783  fabb							;   are gone; walls return on re-entry, D1-B). WallMask (BombPacked b3-6) is
   1784  fabb							;   retired: HotOverlapBody now tests its parent hot cell's PF bit.
   1785  fabb							;   Cost: ≤4 cells × 3 rows × ~3 cell probes; blast edge only.
   1786  fabb							; ========================================================================
   1787  fabb		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FB10 - *, 0
